@kenz1117/dsh-ui-usage-billing README · Eight sections, one consistent ledger：Overview / Queue / Billing / Usage / Trends / Agents / Rates / Settings. The hero and KPIs cover today, 7 days, week, month, all time and custom dates; trends, heatmaps, budgets, rates and searchable settings all read the same real ledger.

<details>
<summary><strong>Queue, agent and settings details</strong></summary>

@kenz1117/dsh-ui-usage-billing README · Eight sections, one consistent ledger：- **Queue**: price-band countdown and queued / running / needs-review / completed tasks; up to 50 JSON items per batch, validated atomically. Locks and leases prevent duplicate submission across instances sharing one `DSH_HOME`.
- **Agents**: a parent conversation → sub-agent tree with own cost and chain total including every descendant.
- **Settings**: full-text search, global and per-model budgets, peak alerts, custom prices, native host settings and plugin information; a hidden sidebar entry can be restored from host Settings.

@kenz1117/dsh-ui-usage-billing README · 🔌 Subscriptions & balance：- **Subscription quotas**: detect Kimi, Z.ai, OpenCode Go, MiniMax, Claude, CommandCode and more, with remaining quota and reset times; subscription-channel model cost is 0.
- **Official balances**: DeepSeek, Kimi, StepFun, SiliconFlow, xAI, Zhipu GLM and Tencent Cloud TokenHub, with days remaining estimated from the last 7 days.
- **Relays and reconciliation**: merge keys by site, read New API / Sub2API rolling quotas, and cross-check custom endpoints or official balance deltas against the ledger.

@kenz1117/dsh-ui-usage-billing README · 🔐 Permissions & Compatibility (DSH STORE)：- **Permission level: high**: reads durable Session logs, calls vendor / subscription / balance / pricing APIs, reads `apiKeyEnv` through the credentials seam, and writes the ledger, snapshots and task queue under the harness home. The plugin itself has **no** command-execution / shell capability; only explicit enqueueing creates a host Session and submits a Prompt, while Agent tools remain governed by the host's existing permissions and approvals.
- **Update channel: `user-reviewed`**: with file / network / credential capabilities, DSH STORE requires local manual confirmation on every install; review the repo, pinned commit, lifecycle scripts, and impact scope before installing.
- **Compatibility**: stable and preview releases from the current `main` share one matrix covering DSH `0.1.2-alpha.1` through `0.2.2-alpha.3`, with 33 per-version declarations. The current stable release is `1.8.2` (npm `latest`); the preview channel is `1.8.3-alpha.1` (npm `alpha`, the Hunyuan Hy4 GA catalog expansion). Release channels and monitoring are documented in [COMPATIBILITY.md](COMPATIBILITY.md). Node.js `^22.19.0

@kenz1117/dsh-ui-usage-billing README · 🤖 Model Experience：| Tool | Parameters | Behaviour |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `usage_stats` | `range`: `today` / `month` / `session` / `all` / `bySite` / `relay` | Queries the usage and estimated cost this plugin already aggregated (CNY, estimated from the official price catalog — not a bill); `session` requires an agent session context |

@kenz1117/dsh-ui-usage-billing README · ⚠️ Known Limitations and Deferred Work：- **The off-peak queue is still a preview**: it accepts only time-of-day models on the host's built-in `deepseek-official` route; relays and custom routes are excluded. There is no automatic pause, cancellation or retry. After host shutdown, a dropped result stream or lease expiry, the task becomes "Needs review"; open its Session and decide manually whether to enqueue a new task.
- **Balance queries cover DeepSeek / Moonshot (Kimi) / StepFun / SiliconFlow / xAI / Zhipu GLM (Z.ai CN region) / Tencent Cloud TokenHub (token-plan quota)**: the first six use a standard Bearer API key; Tencent Cloud uses the cloud-API key pair (`<SecretId>:<SecretKey>`, TC3-signed management API). Other providers expose no public balance API or need non-Bearer auth (Xiaomi MiMo via console Cookie, SenseTime via AccessKey signing, MiniMax/Doubao via quota or AK/SK), so they currently show "not configured"; the extension point is `src/balance.ts` (add a querier per provider balance API).
- **Relay quota depends on upstream private schemas**: New API / Sub2API interface fields are not public, so an unreadable station is labeled
